.IsTwo) ∧ ∃ positive contractions a b, ∀ normalized 2-quasitraces τ, 1/144 ≤ Re(τ(a+b) - τ a - τ b)` (all normalized 2-quasitraces are non-additive), and `stable_finiteness_bundle := SimpleStableTensorCounterexample ∧ ReducedQuasitraceLoss ∧ TraceFreeStablyFinite` (C*_r(F₂) and a simple stably finite M whose spatial tensor product `tensorAlgebra ρ` is `ProperlyInfinite`, plus the quasitrace-loss and trace-free examples). Both parts of the summary are stated.","text":"The challenge statements imply the headline claim after unpacking definitions or one routine step.","url":"https://github.com/mathvet/mathvet/blob/14c7f918cd336d0da03a02aae5a0eed4a429d4db/reviews/openai-math/fidelity-table.csv","verdict":"full"},"source_verdict":"full","state":"all","target":"f:294","target_kind":"family-headline"}],"release_id":"openai-math","remaining_checks":[{"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:574149ccb10d081554aeafd13d3bbc8a174d3cbf3a91d0972e3f4eca895e730c","grain":"challenge","id":"challenge:KaplanskyQuasitrace","title":"KaplanskyQuasitrace"},"kind":"scope-review","reason":"An AI scope draft has no named human review.","target":"l:KaplanskyQuasitrace"},{"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:a06df1b9ad46cdbfd1a10f0dba24a93a29fa61bac527a1e8b10a56ff861061f2","grain":"challenge","id":"challenge:KaplanskyStableFiniteness","title":"KaplanskyStableFiniteness"},"kind":"scope-review","reason":"An AI scope draft has no named human review.","target":"l:KaplanskyStableFiniteness"},{"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:ec024d3b5da6aaebf338a6f9021bb66831b13c068519841911eee444c5bc236c","grain":"family","id":"family:294","title":"Kaplansky's quasitrace conjecture and failure of tensor-product stable finiteness"},"kind":"claim-identification","reason":"Lexical navigation candidate; catalogue headline identity requires review.","target":"f:294"},{"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:ec024d3b5da6aaebf338a6f9021bb66831b13c068519841911eee444c5bc236c","grain":"family","